    {
      "id": "IUyHfL4Od-_OrkrlKEgHA",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 235.67579293027643,
      "y": 1107.8491473279332,
      "width": 359.9397277832031,
      "height": 75,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b1s",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 219643502,
      "version": 249,
      "versionNonce": 2104152406,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1781731918967,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "-- DOM with augmented fake cursors\n-- contenteditable = true\n-- Canvas",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "-- DOM with augmented fake cursors\n-- contenteditable = true\n-- Canvas",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "XPBeGNKzOfaFDNFd7H23g",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 756.7800917505031,
      "y": 1088.6756578194963,
      "width": 764.0594482421875,
      "height": 175,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b1t",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 523012146,
      "version": 851,
      "versionNonce": 6690570,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1781731918967,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "====> The most common approach is \"contenteditable=true\" \nthough Canvas approach is more advance (real google architect)\n1. Design editor-specific model of document content (usually tree-based)\n2. Mapping between model and DOM elements\n3. Define set of supported operations on model (eg: insert, delete, format)\n4. Translate user event (keypress, mouseclick) into sequence of these support\n5. Update DOM based on operational. (DOM update based on model change)",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "====> The most common approach is \"contenteditable=true\" \nthough Canvas approach is more advance (real google architect)\n1. Design editor-specific model of document content (usually tree-based)\n2. Mapping between model and DOM elements\n3. Define set of supported operations on model (eg: insert, delete, format)\n4. Translate user event (keypress, mouseclick) into sequence of these support\n5. Update DOM based on operational. (DOM update based on model change)",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "PYAIJNvbZm-sswC4knihx",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 225.34643261262943,
      "y": 1247.5828685076444,
      "width": 294.81982421875,
      "height": 50,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#2f9e44",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
